    "content": "Ford has recalled over 600,000 vehicles (2020–2022 Explorer, Escape, Lincoln Aviator, and Corsair) due to faulty front wiper motors that can fail, reducing visibility. The issue involves a poorly connected wiper motor brush card. Dealers will replace the wiper motors for free, with owner notification beginning April 2026. This video explains the details of the Ford wiper recall: Affected Vehicles: 2020-2022 Ford Explorer, 2020-2022 Ford Escape, 2020-2022 Lincoln Aviator, and 2020-2022 Lincoln Corsair. Defect: The front wiper motor may fail, leading to reduced visibility and an increased risk of a crash. Remedy: Dealers will replace the wiper motors, free of charge. Action Required: Check your vehicle's VIN on NHTSA.gov to see if your car is affected. NHTSA.gov Contact: Owners can contact Ford customer service at 1-866-436-7332 (mentioning recall #24S51 or #26S14). An earlier, separate recall in 2022 also addressed wiper issues for 2021-2022 F-150 vehicles, focusing on damaged wiper arms.",
